# Build output installed here by `scripts/build.mts`. Committing a 2.5 MB addon
# and two DLLs would put binaries in the repo and guarantee a stale one is
# eventually loaded; `package.json`'s `files` list is what ships them.
aethervfs.node
vfs_shim_dll.dll
vfs_payload.dll

# `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` output, as of the TypeScript migration. The
# sources are `index.cts`, `native.cts` and `provider-host.cts`, and they sit
# beside their outputs — which works only because `.cts` and `.cjs` are different
# extensions, and which keeps `__dirname` meaning the same directory in both.
#
# **`index.d.cts` is in here on purpose.** A hand-written `index.d.ts` used to be
# committed beside a hand-written `index.cjs`; the whole point of task 2 is that
# the declaration is emitted, and a committed copy of a build output is how it
# starts drifting again. `package.json`'s `files` list is what ships it.
index.cjs
index.d.cts
native.cjs
native.d.cts
provider-host.cjs
provider-host.d.cts
*.tsbuildinfo

# The stand-in executable the demo launches. Built, not authored.
fixtures/

# The package has npm **devDependencies** as of the TypeScript migration —
# vitest, typescript and @types/node — and no runtime dependencies, which is the
# part that was always deliberate. `pnpm-lock.yaml` is committed (it is the point
# of `--frozen-lockfile` in CI); `node_modules/` is not.
node_modules/
